WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:04.758
- We're about to meditate
for two months straight.

00:00:04.758 --> 00:00:07.437
- I signed up to do two
months of meditation.

00:00:07.437 --> 00:00:10.310
- I don't really know much
about meditation in general.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:13.368
- So we're going to meditate
for about two months every day

00:00:13.368 --> 00:00:15.856
and see how it goes.

00:00:22.096 --> 00:00:24.612
- Transcendental meditation is one thing.

00:00:24.612 --> 00:00:26.130
It's a mental technique.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:30.681
We always describe it as
simple, natural, and effortless.

00:00:30.681 --> 00:00:32.078
Easy to do.

00:00:32.078 --> 00:00:33.126
And what you're doing is,

00:00:33.126 --> 00:00:36.066
a mental technique which
allows your mind and your body

00:00:36.066 --> 00:00:37.208
to slow down.

00:00:53.458 --> 00:00:55.679
- I'm not a real focused person.

00:00:55.679 --> 00:00:57.304
When I was younger, it was even worse.

00:00:57.304 --> 00:01:00.009
I couldn't even get
through a magazine article

00:01:00.009 --> 00:01:01.797
without losing my concentration.

00:01:01.797 --> 00:01:03.585
- I think I've gotten recently

00:01:03.585 --> 00:01:05.532
way more attached to my phone.

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:07.262
The time that I used to spend

00:01:07.262 --> 00:01:08.908
just with myself and my thoughts

00:01:08.908 --> 00:01:11.574
I now am like, oh I have
some phone time now.

00:01:11.574 --> 00:01:14.398
And so I think it'll just
cut out from my phone time,

00:01:14.398 --> 00:01:15.500
which is great.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:19.063
- I have big anxiety issue.

00:01:19.063 --> 00:01:22.142
I'm basically hoping that meditation

00:01:22.142 --> 00:01:25.325
would help me boost my self-confidence.

00:01:25.325 --> 00:01:28.352
- I have a resting nice face
but a lot of times behind it,

00:01:28.352 --> 00:01:30.647
it's just like panic.

00:01:30.647 --> 00:01:32.455
So my expectation is to be calmer

00:01:32.455 --> 00:01:36.229
and for my mind to race
less, if I could do this.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:37.482
- I'm very excited.

00:01:37.482 --> 00:01:38.592
- I really want it to work.

00:01:38.592 --> 00:01:40.176
- I have to do it.

00:01:45.476 --> 00:01:47.406
- We're here at the
David Lynch Foundation,

00:01:47.406 --> 00:01:50.062
about to start our first day of training.

00:01:50.062 --> 00:01:53.413
- I'm nervous, anxious.

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:57.131
- Last moment says just base,

00:01:57.131 --> 00:01:59.354
terrible human beings.

00:02:10.344 --> 00:02:15.013
- I just got my mantra and,
yeah, I feel really calm.

00:02:15.013 --> 00:02:18.692
- I definitely feel tingly.

00:02:18.692 --> 00:02:19.787
- It felt like such a release,

00:02:19.787 --> 00:02:22.282
I actually started to cry a little bit.

00:02:22.282 --> 00:02:25.274
- It felt like I was on the
bottom of a pool at a party,

00:02:25.274 --> 00:02:26.919
watching the party go on above

00:02:26.919 --> 00:02:30.835
and being super calm and chilled
out underneath the party.

00:02:30.835 --> 00:02:32.201
- That was really interesting,

00:02:32.201 --> 00:02:35.955
I didn't expect to go as
deep as I did right away.

00:02:38.295 --> 00:02:40.642
- I was thinking very visual,

00:02:40.642 --> 00:02:44.099
and there's one point where

00:02:44.099 --> 00:02:47.890
I was, I felt like I
was flying in the wind.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:49.836
- I think I'm going to try
drinking less caffeine,

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:51.907
because I feel like when I
have caffeine in my system

00:02:51.907 --> 00:02:56.840
it makes me harder to
slow down my breathing.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:00.592
- Then I saw a guy with a huge mouth.

00:03:00.592 --> 00:03:02.486
- I'm hopeful, I have to say I'm hopeful,

00:03:02.486 --> 00:03:04.225
and that feels really good.

00:03:04.225 --> 00:03:07.872
- I just went into his
mouth and went inside.

00:03:07.872 --> 00:03:09.526
And it was just pitch black.

00:03:09.526 --> 00:03:10.787
- It's only been two days,

00:03:10.787 --> 00:03:12.936
so very curious to see the changes

00:03:12.936 --> 00:03:15.273
that could take place over two months.

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:19.748
- I've been pretty good.
I've been really good.

00:03:19.748 --> 00:03:22.830
- Probably some of the
best weeks of my life.

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:26.012
- I'm a little bit more chipper.

00:03:26.012 --> 00:03:29.113
- My mid-afternoon stress
headaches went away.

00:03:29.113 --> 00:03:32.353
- I feel much less anxious and
I feel much more like myself,

00:03:32.353 --> 00:03:36.118
like I'm not faking being
relaxed, I actually am relaxed.

00:03:36.118 --> 00:03:38.758
- And I especially love
meditating with my cat.

00:03:41.948 --> 00:03:43.255
(chimes)

00:03:44.752 --> 00:03:48.353
- So last week I went camping
by myself in Joshua Tree.

00:03:48.353 --> 00:03:51.812
I went off trails and I
started climbing boulders.

00:03:51.812 --> 00:03:54.315
I got to the top of really high boulders,

00:03:54.315 --> 00:03:57.644
but one time I could not go back down.

00:03:57.644 --> 00:03:59.529
Just pretty fucking scary.

00:04:02.659 --> 00:04:04.215
And I started to panic.

00:04:05.875 --> 00:04:07.352
This drop...

00:04:07.352 --> 00:04:10.222
I just couldn't find a place
to put my hands or my feet

00:04:10.222 --> 00:04:11.461
and I couldn't go down.

00:04:11.461 --> 00:04:14.998
And if I just jumped down, I'm gonna die.

00:04:14.998 --> 00:04:17.954
My heart's beating really
fast, I could feel it,

00:04:17.954 --> 00:04:19.236
and I was really scared.

00:04:19.236 --> 00:04:22.767
And I told myself, relax, go meditate.

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:25.630
So literally I'm meditating
on top of the boulder.

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:30.073
Couple minutes later I open
my eyes and I felt so calm.

00:04:30.073 --> 00:04:31.697
And easily, I got back down.

00:04:31.697 --> 00:04:35.454
It really relieved my stress and my worry.

00:04:35.454 --> 00:04:37.833
It definitely helped save my life.

00:04:40.595 --> 00:04:43.565
- I feel really good about
transcendental meditation.

00:04:43.565 --> 00:04:46.915
- Meditation had a very
positive impact on my life

00:04:46.915 --> 00:04:49.373
- I'm sad when I don't meditate.

00:04:49.373 --> 00:04:51.632
- It makes me aware of my own company,

00:04:51.632 --> 00:04:55.434
that I can be alone and have
a fulfilling time with myself.

00:04:55.434 --> 00:04:59.383
- When I meditate, I'm
much more in the now.

00:04:59.383 --> 00:05:00.973
- It kinda puts more distance between

00:05:00.973 --> 00:05:03.693
me finding something
out and me freaking out.

00:05:03.693 --> 00:05:06.827
There's another option besides
freak out and be stressed.

00:05:06.827 --> 00:05:10.000
- You know, I was shy, not very confident.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.472
- My anxiety is diminished,

00:05:11.472 --> 00:05:15.596
and my ability to focus on
the task at hand is increased.

00:05:15.596 --> 00:05:20.120
- I think I used to fill
time with trash content,

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:21.792
like Instagram, or Twitter,

00:05:21.792 --> 00:05:25.562
or just constantly stimulating
myself with filler.

00:05:25.562 --> 00:05:28.590
- I think that I will continue
doing this indefinitely,

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:29.768
at least I hope I do.

00:05:29.768 --> 00:05:30.946
- I wanna keep doing it.

00:05:30.946 --> 00:05:35.210
- It's just become so normal
to me, so part of my routine.

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:38.097
- I'm spreading the gospel
of meditation to everybody.

00:05:38.097 --> 00:05:39.532
- It's just there and I love it.

